segments.en:
For the 7 Adar Hilulah of Moshe Rabbeinu &#x05E2;&rdquo;&#x05D4;

Hashem redeems the soul of His servants; and all who take refuge in Him shall not bear guilt [Psalms 34:23]. He has redeemed my soul in peace from the battle that was against me — for the many were with me [Psalms 55:19]. But G&#8209;d shall redeem my soul from the hand of the grave — for He shall receive me, Selah [Psalms 49:16]. My lips shall sing for joy when I sing praises to You — and my soul which You have redeemed [Psalms 71:23]. Master of the Universe — full of mercy; King Who redeems and saves; Who ransoms and rescues and sustains and answers and has mercy at every time of distress and anguish: we have no king except You. Have mercy upon us for the sake of Your Name — through Your many and great mercies; and illuminate upon us a time of favor always through the merit of our holy fathers. And sweeten and nullify all the judgments from upon us and from upon all Your people the House of Israel; and redeem our souls from all the decrees and judgments that have been decreed in all Your twenty-four holy Heavenly Courts [esrim v'arba batei dineinu] — whether before the decree is finalized or whether after the decree is finalized. From all of them may You redeem our souls; and sweeten and nullify all the judgments and sufferings and decrees that have been decreed in them upon us and upon all Your people the House of Israel — whether in body or in soul or in money; whether in general or in particular. For it is revealed and known before You that there is none among us who knows at all how to perform a redemption [pidyon] and to nullify all the judgments decreed in Your holy Courts; and even one who knows how to perform some redemption to nullify some judgment of some Court — still does not know how to nullify all the judgments of all twenty-four Courts. And because of this his redemption avails not. Therefore have mercy upon us through the power and the merit of the great and awesome singular tzadikim of their generations — who are in the aspect of Moshe our master; who have the power to perform a redemption to nullify all the judgments of all twenty-four Courts. And have pity and compassion upon us through the power and merit of these tzadikim; and illuminate upon us the forehead of favor always — as on Shabbos at Minchah [b'Shabbos b'Minchah]; which is the time of the passing of Moshe [histalkus Moshe] — which is the time of favor [eis ratzon]. And through this may You redeem our souls and save us from all troubles; and sweeten and nullify all the decrees and judgments decreed in all Your twenty-four holy Courts. And save us from all manner of illnesses and pains and ailments (and in particular for so-and-so son of so-and-so); and from lack of livelihood and from all manner of grief and suffering in the world. From all of them save us through Your many and great mercies — through the power and merit of Moshe our master who passed on Shabbos at Minchah; and through the power of all the tzadikim who are in the aspect of Moshe — who know how to perform a redemption to sweeten the judgment in all twenty-four Courts.

And arouse Your great mercies and Your abundant lovingkindnesses; and break and demolish and subdue and uproot and nullify all the heresies from all the entire world — and in particular from all Your people the House of Israel wherever they may be. And through Your abundant mercies may You arouse and draw down a time of favor in the world always; and transform the time of apostasy [shemad] to favor [ratzon] — through the power and merit of Moshe who stands between apostasy and favor; who surrendered his soul all the days of his life to make converts [gerim] — to take them out from apostasy and heresy and to raise them and to bind them to the supernal will [ratzon ha'elyon]. And even now after his passing — he still stands and prays for all the estranged and the distant from Your faith; to convert them and to draw them close to You and to nullify all the sectarianism and heresies from the world; and to raise up from apostasy to favor; and to make many converts and penitents [ba'alei teshuvah] in the world.
